Grep and Egrep Practice

Introduction

This project demonstrates the basic usage of "grep" and "egrep" commands in Linux. These commands are used to search and filter text from files.

Sample Data

File: "GREP AND EGREP"

Rahul 85
Amit 72
Priya 90
Rohit 65
Pooja 88
Akash 55

Grep Commands

Search for a specific name:

grep Rahul students.txt

Case-insensitive search:

grep -i rahul students.txt

Search for a specific mark:

grep 90 students.txt

Egrep Commands

Find names starting with R:

egrep "^R" students.txt

Find names starting with A or P:

egrep "^(A|P)" students.txt

Find students with marks between 80 and 99:

egrep "8[0-9]|9[0-9]" students.txt

Learning Outcome

- Understand text searching in Linux.
- Learn case-sensitive and case-insensitive searches.
- Use regular expressions with egrep.
- Filter data efficiently from text files.

